# 105blackmagic_disable_c_xml_target_desc.patch
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# ---------------------
# Target description XML (target.xml) and memory map XML (memory-map.xml) are now
# generated directly on the Rust side (swindle/rs/rs_swindle/src/target_xml.rs and
# memory_map_xml.rs) in zero-heap streaming fashion.
#
# The legacy C implementations in Blackmagic:
# - cortexm_build_target_description() / cortexm_target_description()
# - riscv_build_target_description() / riscv_target_description()
# - mem_map_ram() / mem_map_flash() / target_mem_map_chunk()
# - target_regs_description()
# are no longer called and used heap allocations (malloc) and format strings that
# bloated the firmware binary.
#
# FIX
# ---
# 1. In cortexm.c:
#    - #if 0 the SPR/SYS/TrustZone XML descriptor tables and static asserts.
#    - Update target_is_cortexm() to check target->attach == cortexm_attach instead of regs_description.
#    - Comment out target->regs_description = cortexm_target_description in cortexm_probe().
#    - #if 0 cortexm_build_target_fpu_description, cortexm_build_target_secext_description,
#      cortexm_build_target_description, and cortexm_target_description.
#
# 2. In riscv_debug.c:
#    - #if 0 the GPR/CSR/FPU XML descriptor tables and static assert.
#    - Comment out forward declaration of riscv_target_description.
#    - Comment out target->regs_description = riscv_target_description in riscv_debug_probe().
#    - #if 0 riscv_build_target_fpu_description, riscv_build_target_description,
#      and riscv_target_description.
#
# 3. In target.c:
#    - #if 0 map_begin and map_end strings.
#    - #if 0 mem_map_ram, mem_map_flash, and target_mem_map_chunk.
#    - #if 0 target_regs_description.
#
